This is an example code to generate a FCC crystal in periodic space and then shear it, replicating the model presented in Thornton, C. (1979). The conditions for failure of a face-centered cubic array of uniform rigid spheres. Géotechnique, 29(4), 441-459. https://doi.org/10.1680/geot.1979.29.4.441

The model only really works with periodic boundaries since the use of flat plates changes the coordination number, reducing the number of contacts for each particle near the borders.

The fixfree method is used to let contacts develop across the perioic boundaries (i.e. free particles) despite their fixity status.
